{
  "review": "There is a clever little scene in The Karen Carpenter Story, where both Carpenters are in a recording studio, and Richard makes an impromptu decision to have Karen sing for the owner of the studio.<br /><br />Richard picks the wrong key for Karen to sing in, so Karen is singing above her natural range. You can see a look of bemusement on the owner's face; he figures she really can't sing. Richard quickly realizes his mistake and tries again in a different key. The next thing you hear is Karen's amazing, beautiful voice, and the owner does a priceless double take. Nicely done! For some reason, I have never forgotten that scene.<br /><br />The Karen Carpenter Story chronicles the meteoric rise of the Carpenters, and Karen's struggle to overcome anorexia. A lot of things are glossed over. This isn't a documentary, and the movie left me with a lot of questions. Very little is mentioned of Karen's solo venture (the CD was released only a few years ago. If you buy it, you will wonder why they waited. It's some of Karen's best work. The songs aren't as timeless as her work with brother Richard, but it was a great recording, in my opinion).<br /><br />I have heard it said that, you can be listening to a cheap, time-worn little radio in the middle of the Third World, that would seem to produce more static than anything else. But when a Carpenter song comes on the radio, you would think you were listening to a $1000 Hi-Fidelity unit.<br /><br />Watch this movie!",
  "translate": "Ci sono un piccolo ma sorprendente scena nel The Karen Carpenter Story, dove entrambi i Karntons sono in una stereoattedoria e Richard decide imposto al momento stesso di far fare a Karen cantare per l Possessore della stereo.<br /><br />Richard scelge la 错误的键 per far fare a Karen a cantare sopra le sue portate naturali. puoi vedere un espressione di disprezone sull'owner della stereo; convinceva che lei potrebbe essere veramente in grado di non singolarci. Richard subisce rapidamente una comprensione del suo errore e provve a provare nuovamente con un'altra tonalit脿. Il prossimo canto che ascolto Ã¨ la voce di Karen straordinaria, e lo scontrino dell'owner Ã¨ un sor piano double.<br />Buona! Per qualche ragione, non ho dimenticato quella scena.<br /><br />Il The Karen Carpenter Story chronicla il salto marroccano del Karnters, e l'abbazia di Karen per superare la soffitta. molte cose sono passate sotto lo strafo. Non Ã¨ un documentario; e il film mi ha lasciato con tante domande. poco si dice riguardo all'-unit脿 singolo di Karen (il CD Ã¨ stato rilasciato soltanto pochi anni fa. Se ne comprai, avresti capito perchÃ© sono passati i tempi. Ã¨ alcuni dei migliori lavori di Karen. I cantanti non sono tasi assolute come i suoi lavori col fratello Richard, ma era un'ottima registrazione, in mio parere).<br /><br />Ho sentito dire che, puoi essere inoltraggio a un vecchio e ingiallgato radio sul terroir del Mondo Terroso, e sentirebbe piuttosto static. Ma quando un canzone di Carpenter compare sulla radio, si pensa a un $1000 Hi-Fidelity unit.<br /><br />Guarda questo film!",
  "sentiment": "positive"
}

{
  "review": "so all along the season, i got so caught up in school and my activities that i didn't realize that the show had been canceled halfway through, which is a real letdown.<br /><br />i think the fans of this show should ask fox to at least finish filming the remaining episodes so that the season can be released on DVD later. maybe then they'll see how many people were disappointed that the show didn't make it through its first season.<br /><br />i loved the show and looked forward to it every thursday after the oc. can you imagine my disappointment when i came back to try and watch the show only to discover that it had disappeared? needless to say, i'm not very happy with fox right now. even more so after discovering that NO ENDING WAS FILMED. i mean, if you're going to work on a project, at least finish it to see what happens. a half filmed show is like a half made car, it's pretty much useless. fox, film the damn ending and give some of the show's fans some peace.",
