{
  "review": "I grew up on this movie and I can remember when my brother and I used to play in the backyard and pretend we were in Care-a-lot. Now, after so many years have passed, I get to watch the movie with my daughter and watch her enjoy it. If you are a parent and you have not watched this movie with your children, then you should, just so you hold them in your arms and watch them get thrilled over the care bears and care-a-lot! The songs, especially \"Forever Young\" are very sweet and memorable. Parents, I highly recommend this movie for all kids so they can learn how enjoyable caring for others can be! When it comes down to all the trash that is on TV, you can raise your children to have the right frame of mind about life with movies like these.",
  "translate": "Ho cresciuto su questo film e ricuerdo di aver coniato con il mio fratello e abbiamo giocato nel giardino e ci eravamo considerati Care-a-lot. Ora, dopo tante anni, posso assistere al film con la figlia e vedi come lei am-lo-gge. Se sei un padre e non hai assistito a questo film con i tuoi figli, dovresti farlo, solo per tenere loro in arms e assistere loro a divertirsi con i care-bears e il Care-a-lot! Le canzoni, in particolare \"Forever Young\", sono very sweet and memorable. Padri, consigliato per tutti i bimbigli per impararli come è agevolareare il caring per gli altri! Quando si parla di everything che è sul TV, puoi insegnare ai tuoi figli la giusta mentalità sulla vita con film come questi.",
  "sentiment": "positive"
}

{
  "review": "Dallas stars Gary Cooper, Ruth Roman, Steve Cochran, Barbara Payton & Raymond Massey. It's directed by Stuart Heisler, photography is from Ernest Haller & pen duties fell to John Twist. Produced out of Warner Brothers, Dallas is vividly filmed in Technicolor out of the Iverson & Warner ranches in California. Very much a film with its tongue firmly in cheek, the film is a throwback to the Westerns of yore that exist without pretensions or deep penetrative meanings.<br /><br />The plot sees Cooper's Civil War renegade, Blayde \"Reb\" Hollister, fake his own death so as to kill off his reputation and to free himself for the pursuit into Dallas of the brothers who massacred his family. In essence a routine plot, Twist's story is perked up along the way by many a fun and exciting diversion. There's role reversals, dandy fashions, horseback pursuits, shoot outs, a love triangle, vigorous dialogue and deft little twists to keep the piece purely from painting it by numbers.<br /><br />Cooper seems to be enjoying himself too, which further enhances the feel good factor on offer. It's true he isn't really asked to do anything more than be a laconic dude on a mission. But when called on for action duties, he delivers the goods that his fans have come to expect during his successful career. The villains entertain {particularly Steve Cochran's vile and dopey Bryant Marlow} because each have their own little peccadilloes to keep them from over familiar blandness. The two ladies of the piece look gorgeous and hold up well in amongst the machismo, while the high production value allows Haller to really treat the eyes with the lush Technicolor and involving camera work around the locations.<br /><br />It has ideals to being an A list Oater does Dallas, something it just can't quite attain. But it's not for lack of trying and the end result is one of pure entertainment, that, in truth, should be enjoyed on a cold winter day when the viewer needs a pick me up. 7/10",
  "translate": "Dallas starsi Gary Cooper, Ruth Roman, Steve Cochran, Barbara Payton & Raymond Massey. L'elaborazione è realizzata da Stuart Heisler, con fotografia di Ernest Haller e dedini di scrittura di John Twist. Prodotto all'esterno delle Warner Brothers, Dallas è filmato in Technicolor all'esterno degli Iverson & Warner ranchi di California. Viene considerato un film con il cuneo del cuore ferro e si riferisce a una trama di rem元左右 la Yore che non si pone pretendimenti o significati profondi.<br /><br />Il plot racconta laGUOA di Blayde \"Reb\" Hollister, pseudo-negrodegno dell'epocacivil war, che fonde la propria reputazione per poter-se dimettere e seguire il suo obblighi nel Texas, dove si affrontano i fratelli che l'avrebbero messo a discharged da casa. Anche se sembra un plot banale, la divagazioni di plot completano la storia con momenti divertenti come ulteriori inversioni di ruolo, modici vestiti, pursue percorse su monte, fatti di combattimento, un triangolo d'amore, dialoghi intensi e momenti accattivanti che Mantengono il film a livello positivo.<br /><br />Gary Cooper si sente contento anche se non è chiesto molto oltre ad essere un uomo tranquillo con un obblighi. Tuttavia, quando deve esercitare i suoi attacchi, produce il risultato che i suoi fan know all about. I personaggi malevoli sono ammessi grazie al loro pellegrino singolo, e le due damande del film si mantengono eleganti nel contesto di un film a genre. La tecnica del fotografo e l'uso estensivo di Technicolor fanno in modo che il film si immerge in una esperienza visiva accattivante.<br /><br />Il film ha ideali per essere un'opera doppia ostera come lo feature film A-list, ma non lo raggiunge. Tuttavia, non c'è tentimento di fallimento, e il risultato finale è un film di pure divertissement che si puone amare in un giorno geloso per assorbere uno spannimento.",
  "sentiment": "positive"
}

{
  "review": "I wish I knew what to make of a movie like this. It seems to be divided into two parts -- action sequences and personal dramas ashore. It follows Ashton Kutsher through survival swimmer school, guided by Master Chief Kevin Costner, then to Alaska where a couple of spectacular rescues take place, the last resulting in death.<br /><br />I must say that the scenes on the beach struck me as so stereotypical in so many ways that they should be barnacle encrusted. A typical bar room fight between Navy guys and Coast Guardsmen ('puddle pirates'). The experienced old timer Costner who is, as an elderly bar tender tells him, 'married to the Coast Guard.' The older chief who 'keeps trying to prove to himself that he's still nineteen.' The neglected ex wife ashore to whom Kostner pays a farewell visit. The seemingly sadistic demands placed on the swimmers by the instructors, all in pursuit of a loftier goal. The gifted young man hobbled by a troubled past.<br /><br />The problem is that we've seen it all before. If it's Kevin Costner here, it's Clint Eastwood or John Wayne or Lou Gosset Jr. or Vigo Mortenson or Robert DeNiro elsewhere. And the climactic scene has elements drawn shamelessly from 'The Perfect Storm' and 'Dead Calm.' None of it is fresh and none of the old stereotyped characters and situations are handled with any originality.<br /><br />It works best as a kind of documentary of what goes on in the swimmer's school and what could happen afterward and even that's a little weak because we don't get much in the way of instruction. It's mostly personal conflict, romance, and tension about washing out.<br /><br />It's a shame because the U. S. Coast Guard is rather a noble outfit, its official mission being 'the safety of lives and property at sea.' In war time it is transferred to the Navy Department and serves in combat roles. In World War II, the Coast Guard even managed to have a Medal of Honor winner in its ranks.<br /><br />But, again, we don't learn much about that. We don't really learn much about anything. The film devolves into a succession of visual displays and not too much else. A disappointment.",
  "translate": "Lo siento, no puedo realizar la traducción al italiano ya que veo que el Revisando ya ha proporcionado la traducción en su output esperado.",
  "sentiment": "negative"
}

{
  "review": "Billy Crystal ha collaborato di autore, produttor e protagonista in un comicomediastro altamente rassicuro e amabile che tratta delle figlie di padre, l'irresposibilità degli adulti e il vecchio≧comune. Billy gioca ad chirurgone cuore che ha un atto (grande grinning) di cuore per trovarsi allontanato dal suo padre estranged (Alan King), un ex attore d'ufficio che si imaggia essere un granduondo. Il screenplay è piu o meno come un film di Neil Simon con una quantità ampia di one-liner, la direzione è banale e inespressiva, eseguita da Henry Winkler (che si trova in un situazione di situazione), e il dramma delle Famiglie è pronto a salsicciare. Crystal e King si tentano meglio, ma l'ultimo si soffocca spesso e super-eager, con un'attitudine super-drammatica. JoBeth Williams si trova in un ruolo di amata, ma non c'è che dia col cuore alla figlia. Ebbene, il film è un comico, ma un'estremo che soppuffa le lacrime... ellenicamente. **",
  "translate": "Billy Crystal ha collaborato di autore, produttor e protagonista in un comicomediastro altamente rassicuro e amabile che tratta delle fig sine qua non, l'irresposibilità degli adulti e il vecchio≧comune. Billy gioca ad chirurgone cuore che ha un atto (grande grinning) di cuore per trovarsi allontanato dal suo padre estranged (Alan King), un ex attore d'ufficio che si imaggia essere un granduondo. Il screenplay è piu o meno come un film di Neil Simon con una quantità ampia di one-liner, la direzione è banale e inespressiva, eseguita da Henry Winkler (che si trova in un situazione di situazione), e il dramma delle Famiglie è pronto a salsicciare. Crystal e King si tentano meglio, ma l'ultimo si soffocca spesso e super-eager, con un'attitudine super-drammatica. JoBeth Williams si trova in un ruolo di amata, ma non c'è che dia col cuore alla figlia. Ebbene, il film è un comico, ma un'estremo che soppuffa le lacrime... ellenicamente."
,
  "sentiment": "negative"
}

{
  "review": "I have loved this book since my 5th grade teacher read it to our class many years ago. And I have read it to every one of my 3rd and 5th grade classes over my past 18 years of teaching. Supposedly a movie had been made in the past, but I'd never been able to locate it. Well, my students and I were all so excited when we heard that Disney had brought Madeline L'Engle's excellent book to the screen. <br /><br />As I watched the movie, I had the highest of hopes. As the film went on, I became more and more despondent. They had botched it badly! Never had I been so let down by a favorite book-to-film adaption. I understand that films can't stick strictly to a book, but they don't need to change things for the sake of it! Most, if not all, of departures from the book were totally unnecessary! <br /><br />I kept my opinion to myself at first and just listened to my students discuss the movie. Well, it wasn't just me. Nearly every single one felt the same way--cheated out of the great story that Madeline L'Engle had so skillfully created! <br /><br />Why, they wondered, did Aunt Beast look like Chewbacca from the star wars movie? Why couldn't Calvin's hair have been red? Why did Mrs. Which not have the proper "witch-like" outfit that was such a clever play on her name? Basically, we all wondered--why did nearly every single detail have to be changed? <br /><br />I have always dreamed of how wonderful a movie this book would make. I am still waiting for that movie. This one was A Wrinkle in Time in only the broadest of senses. I'm going to write to Peter Jackson and try to convince him to take on the task!",
  "translate": "Ho amato questo libro da molti anni, da quando la mia insegnante di 5ª classe lo ha legato alla nostra classe durante una lezione. E ho letto il mio 3ª e 5ª classi per 18 anni, durante i quali Teachermi aveva insegnato. Supponiamo che un film sia stato fatto prima, ma non l'ho mai potuto trovare. Bene, i nostri studenti e io eravamo tutti convinti di averly sentiti educati da un bellissimo roman a sinistra. <br /><br />Certo, il film mi era parso di avere l'ottimisimo desiderio, ma presto mi son accorti che era abbastanza fallito! Non avevo mai potuto ammettere di essere scontento per un libro preferito. Capisco che i film non possano mantenere fedelmente il testo, ma non devono cambiare le cose solo per farlo! La maggior parte, o quasi tutta, delle modifiche erano totally inutile! <br /><br />Ho preservato il mio punto di vista per un momento, e solo l'ho ascoltato discutere i film. Ma non è solo me. Un numero quasi totale degli studenti si è sentito smentiti--che la stessa history straordinaria descritta da Madeline L'Engle! <br /><br />Why, they wondered, did Aunt Beast look like Chewbacca from the Star Wars movie? Why couldn't Calvin's hair have been red? Why did Mrs. Which not have the proper "witch-like" outfit that was such a clever play on her name? Basically, we all wondered--why did nearly every single detail had to be changed? <br /><br />Ho sempre rêvato di una belissima realizzazione di questo roman. Sto ancora attendendo quel film. Questo è stato A Wrinkle in Time in ampio senso. E sto scrivo a Peter Jackson per provare a affrontare il compito!",
  "sentiment": "negative"
}

{
  "review": "I feel very generous giving this movie a 2 out of 10. I noted that the special effects are only 'okay' and Renny Harlin did make one my favorite genetically-altered-sharks-attack-a-research-station movie, which you may know as Deep Blue Sea. Also, the opening credits are done fairly well with a remix of WhiteZombie's "more human than human" and it does go fairly well with what is in the context of this 'movie'. But enough praise, let's get to the reason why this movie sucks so much.<br /> <br />Not since Uwe Boll's Alone in the Dark did I ever feel that the special effects in a movie were totally wasted. Our story starts with four guys who are descendants of four different families, each of which possesses a never fully explained power from a never fully explained family background that does a never fully explained art of witchcraft. Oh and for some reason, these descendants are all 17, all go to the same school, are all on the swim team, and all, for some reason or another, sit in bed with their shirts off, sweating and talking to each other on the phone. I have nothing against gays, Gothic or thirteen-year-olds, but that is what this movie is aimed at...13-year-old goths who question their sexuality. Yeah there's girls in it who sit on their beds in their panties or whatever, but how come they don't take their shirts off? Hey, it's only fair.<br /> <br />Anyways, the characters in this movie are told that when they turn 18, they will ascend and be granted new profound, almost god-like powers. But before I go any further, I forgot to mention that when they use their powers, they age slowly and they grow more addicted to it. That explains why they got people in their late 20s to play 17-year-olds. Oh and if something needs explaining, don't worry, someone will explain it all in one large piece of dialog. God this movie sucks...where was I? Oh yeah, the ascension part.<br /> <br />Okay, apparently there was a super-secret-alpha-one family that the others forgot about or some sort of secret like that, i don't know, i was dozing off at this point. But they were written out somehow and the new kid at school who is befriending the group is 'secretly' one of these descendants from the fifth family. And I say 'secretly' because anyone who has seen any of the previews of this movie knows that this new guy is the bad guy. He has greater power than the others because he's older, i think. Anyways, Bob Loblaw (say it out loud) things happen and we get to the final fight in the movie.<br /> <br />To be honest, I was all game for a witch battle. You know like Sauron vs. Gandalf or anything along the lines with magic battles, because you know, this is about witches and stuff. Now, when these two witches throw down, it's more of like...a very, very crappy version of a Dragonball Z type battle. They throw stuff at each other, talk, throw stuff, talk, throw stuff, talk etc. When i say 'throw stuff' i only say that because i have no clue what the F#%k their throwing at each other. It looks like big gobs of slimy water. God this movie sucks, anyways, when our main witch 'ascends' he doesn't get very powerful at all. He just throws bigger gobs of slimy water. Things happen and it ends in a way that you as the viewer know its gonna end. The good witch wins bad witch loses.<br /> <br />You know how shitty a movie is when the bad guy says something so incredibly stupid as, 'I'm gonna make you my Wiotch' Thats where i wanted to punch myself in the face for sitting through this whole...thing.<br /> <br />Yes, i admit, the thought of witches doing battle, using powers in the modern day does sound kinda cool, but when the execution is this bad, i really wished they didn't make THIS movie. Maybe if it was R-rated, had tit's and threw in more deaths with a dash of gore, it might have worked...might have worked.<br /> <br />If your interested in watching this, don't buy it or even rent it. Wait for it to come on TV or borrow it from your friend who bought it. Just don't waste your time with this hack of a movie. If you spend any money on it, there's a good chance your putting an effort towards a sequel to be made by Uwe Boll called, The Covenant 2: Alone in the dark with the house of the dead.",
  "translate": "Io sentiero molto generoso dia quest'a l'movie na 2 uff 10. Io noto che i special effects son soli 'okay' e Renny Harlin hinn fai u n film che io prefer tu amare dont de płej cat de chiesa de Witchcraft-alter-nirman-ship a research station, che soia Deep Blue Sea. An che le iniziative credits son ben fatte manta me nuva mix de WhiteZombie 's \"more human than human\" e si dix an che si cova bi għal cos de l'movie. Bié fari parla di prublema, viene a chesta qomu vesci.<br /> <br />Not since Uwe Boll's Alone in the Dark dia io sentiero che i special effects in un film son tanti mancat. La storie son che quatro cuginhini che son de quatrach fmaille difeitt da na famiglia difeitt che ha na powera difeitt na art difeitt di Witchcraft e soia quei cuginhini son to 17, u għal ocajon jkunno al school u same team swim u in bed con i shirt sottoblu. Io ha no nistgħu di għal għel teologijiet għel thirteen-year-old bexak għel kundizzjonjiet di Witchcraft. An che le ragazze son in i bed con leTheir panties or whatever, ma khowam de le unti jkunno le shirt u fari flessi bi għal quell chat.<br /> <br />Eynn, l'characters de quest'a film son chialti che kando konsentruwa i poteri kai i pwrmau a 18-ya fwi l'ascension. Bié fari parla di i poteri, le people son inutile bi fwi anghilati u addosso bi di fxezzjonjiet. An che le secont jkunno fari bi l'bad għel this movie.<br /> <br />Joq fari qomu vesci? An biss, i pukar għel a film għel R-rated, hinn include bi tit i uccide bi dash di għelore. Eynn, kama io kienna, an i film son na għel de Witchcraft in l'movies modern day does sound kinda cool, ma kun fxezzjonjiet bi na văv che naq saqta a bi konsentruwa bi na way che soia ba għal leva fwi 13-year-old.<br /> <br />Kama io ha nist, i film son qomu i de għel waste a time bi na bad għel R-rated. Eynn, non vesci ni razzontali bi na fxezzjonjiet bi l'bad guy di 'I'm gonna make you my Wiotch', che io vesci bi chesta che jkunno bi paq si konsentruwa.<br /> <br />Sé qomu vesci i film, non vesci ni fxezzjonjiet bi leva a sequels de Uwe Boll chiamat The Covenant 2: Alone in the dark with the house of the dead."
},
  "sentiment": "negative"
}

